# r1115 phase 3 (runner-3), boot A1: SQ-MELT Melting system on the installed jars (NOSWAP=1), superflat level p3a1.
# Server: NOSWAP=1 bash tools/scratch_query/prep_srv.sh OUT p3a1 A difficulty=normal
# Before boot: copy zmelt_probe.js, zp_probe.js into OUT/srv/kubejs/server_scripts as zz_zmelt_probe.js, zz_zp_probe.js.
# Layout: every target and source sits in a 1-deep pit at y -61 (grass replaced, dirt floor), so melt water stays put.
#   Cases at least 12 blocks apart. Bot m3 (survival) at 2060 -60 2060 keeps the area random-ticking (no player = no
#   random ticks); m3n does the same on a stone platform on the Nether roof (y 128, 0..31). Night, clear, doFireTick off.
# Generated by tools/scratch_query/melt_gen_p3.py; edit there.
pace 0.5

## P3-00 | setup (not a queue row): forceload, rules, bots, Nether platform
> forceload add 1984 1984 2143 2143
> execute in minecraft:the_nether run forceload add 0 0 31 31
> gamerule doFireTick false
> gamerule doMobSpawning false
> gamerule doDaylightCycle false
> time set 18000
> weather clear 1000000
> gamerule randomTickSpeed 3
> execute in minecraft:the_nether run fill 0 128 0 31 128 31 minecraft:stone
> execute in minecraft:the_nether run fill 0 129 0 31 133 31 minecraft:air
sleep 5
> pbot spawn m3 2060 -60 2060 minecraft:overworld survival
> pbot spawn m3n 8 129 8 minecraft:the_nether survival
sleep 3
expect bot m3 at
expect bot m3n at

## SQ-MELT-10 | boot log: [melting] tags fire >= 100, source-driven magma only, no low-light warning; fire tag ids
bootexpect \[melting\] tags: \d+ meltable
bootexpect \[melting\] random ticks on for \d+ extra blocks
bootreject fire tag blocks with light below
shell grep -hE "\[melting\]" logs/latest.log | sed -E 's/^.*\[melting\]/[melting]/' | cut -c1-400
> zq blocktag creativecommon:melting/fire
> zq blocktag creativecommon:melting/salt
> zq blocktag creativecommon:melting/lava
> zq blocktag creativecommon:melting/meltable
> zq blocktag creativecommon:melting/meltable_slow
waitlog blocktag creativecommon:melting/meltable_slow 30
look fire count >= 100 in the [melting] tags line; source-driven list = magma_block (light 3) only; every 3.8 table id in the blocktag fire line

